# Docker
# Broadened (#275) to cover docker/Dockerfile.e2e and the e2e compose file,
# which the old root-only list still shipped into every build context.
#
# NOT `docker/` wholesale: docker/Dockerfile:122 COPYs docker-entrypoint.sh and
# healthcheck.sh out of that directory, so excluding it breaks every image
# build. Only the Dockerfiles and compose files are excluded — and those are
# read by the client, never needed inside the context.
Dockerfile*
docker/Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
docker/docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore

# Derived test artifacts (#275) — large, regenerated constantly, and never
# needed by a build; leaving them in busts the cache on every test run.
#
# `tests/` is deliberately NOT excluded, despite the audit suggesting it:
# Dockerfile.e2e does `COPY . .` and runs `pnpm test:e2e` from the image with no
# bind mount, so dropping the suites would leave that image with nothing to run.
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
coverage/

# Generated output that is already gitignored (#275). `.dockerignore` does NOT
# read `.gitignore`, so every one of these was still being shipped into the
# build context — 677M of it, on a context that measured 1.19GB.
#
# Each is regenerated inside the image or never used by it:
#   out/               `pnpm run build` produces it; strip-css-script-tags.mjs
#                      then reads it from THAT build, not from the host copy
#   sites/_warehouse/  baked GLB/atlas artifacts; no build step reads them
#                      (the 2 tracked sites/*.json configs are kept)
#   screenshots/       debug captures. NOT the PWA screenshots — those live in
#                      public/screenshots/ and are referenced by
#                      generate-manifest.js, which only writes URL strings
#   graphify-out/      knowledge-graph artifacts, tooling only
#   storybook-static/  a build output of its own
/out/
sites/_warehouse/
screenshots/
graphify-out/
storybook-static/

# Generated DOT-directories (#275). These dominate the context — .pnpm-store
# alone is ~1.3GB — and were missed on the first pass because `du -sh ./*` does
# not match dotfiles. All five are gitignored with zero tracked files.
#
# Measure the context, do not eyeball it: BuildKit transfers incrementally, so a
# second build reports only the delta and looks tiny regardless of what is
# excluded. Read `transferring context` on a COLD builder.
.pnpm-store/
.chatt-verify/
.speckit-tools/
.speckit-cache/